        <body>
            <div xml:id="d465">

                <pb facs="0691" n="675" xml:id="pg675"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">861.24/4–647: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the Soviet Union</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Smith</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret   urgent</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Moscow</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1947-04-06T16:00:00+03:00">April 6, 1947—4 p.
                            m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1216. Embtel 1201, April 5. When I called on
                    Molotov, I presented <hi rendition="#italic">aide-mémoire</hi> outlining remarks
                    I made. Substance follows:</p>
                <p>Pointed out we have requested commencement negotiations settlement lend-lease
                    more than four times with no results; reminded him of my prediction in February
                    that matter was rapidly becoming political question in US, adding that now this
                    prediction has been borne out, that matter now in hands of appropriations
                    committees and pending Congressional consideration, pipeline shipments stopped.
                    Informed him that if in few days favorable reply not received, Executive Branch
                    would have to inform Congress officially of failure to obtain Soviet consent to
                    negotiation of settlement and added that such failure might have unfavorable
                    reaction on US–Soviet trade relations.</p>
                <p>Favorable Soviet reply outlined my reference telegram.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Smith</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
